 "wfp_results": {
  "filter_counts_before_during_after_all_6_runs": "1008 / 1016 / 1008",
  "delta": "8 new filters per launch, present only in the during capture, all 8 absent in the after capture; before and after key sets identical; no filter removed during a launch; filter keys differ per run (review 0edfd824, independent parser over the raw XML)",
  "mxc_named_filter_count_from_the_state_snapshot": "0 before and after in 6 of 6 (the snapshot is read before and after a launch and the per-launch filters exist only during it, so 0 does not bear on them; the four Tessera filters are Windows-named, the two MXC-Loopback filters are MXC-named)",
  "six_filters_keyed_to_the_run_package": "per launch, FWPM_CONDITION_ALE_PACKAGE_ID equal to that run's AppContainer SID (equal to the in-container token readback): 4 Windows Tessera filters (name 'Tessera Sandbox Filter', ALE_AUTH_CONNECT v4 and v6, one PERMIT and one BLOCK each; provider 'Tessera Sandbox Provider' {2f8c6d14-3b7e-4a59-9c08-1d4e7a6b2f30}, sublayer 'Tessera Sandbox SubLayer' {7b1e9a2c-9d4f-4c8a-b321-5e6d2f8a1c44}, weight 65533) and 2 Windows Firewall service (mpssvc app-isolation) filters 'Sandbox.{GUID}' (ALE_AUTH_RECV_ACCEPT v4 and v6, PERMIT)",
  "two_filters_that_only_mention_the_run_sid": "per launch, 2 mpssvc filters named 'MXC-Loopback' (ALE_AUTH_RECV_ACCEPT v4 and v6, PERMIT) whose PACKAGE_ID is a different, constant package SID (S-1-15-2-2397545170-..., the same in all 6 runs, absent from the before and after state) and which carry the run SID only inside a remote-user security descriptor",
  "constant_package_sid_owner": "the constant SID is the AppContainer SID derived from the name MXC-Loopback (SHA-256 of the lower-cased UTF-16LE name, first 28 bytes read as seven little-endian uint32; the derivation reproduces all seven sub-authorities, and the same computation on a Store package name reproduces that package's SID in the run records' AppContainer mappings). MXC-Loopback is MXC's own identifier: in microsoft/mxc 525d0f25, base_container_helpers.rs:24 defines LOOPBACK_NETWORK_PEER as 'MXC-Loopback', used at :176 and base_container_runner.rs:3231,3441, and docs/backends/process-container/networking.md:121-124 says that in proxy mode the host-loopback setting 'selects both the networkLoopback capability and the MXC-Loopback peer'; the ASCII string is in MXC's wxc-exec.exe and mxc_ffi.dll. The four app-isolation filters (the 2 Sandbox.{GUID} filters keyed to the run package, carrying the MXC-Loopback SID in their remote-user descriptor, and the 2 MXC-Loopback filters carrying the run SID) are one reciprocal loopback peering between the run container and MXC's named peer, installed by the Windows Firewall service (FWPM_PROVIDER_MPSSVC_APP_ISOLATION), not by MXC code. That MXC requests the peer through its process security environment spec is the source's statement, not observed here.",
  "tessera_permit": "same two conditions plus remote address 127.0.0.1/32 (::1/128 for v6), IP protocol 6, remote port 18110 (the configured proxy port); weight 8",
  "tessera_block": "no address, port or protocol condition: every outbound connect from the package; weight 1; same sublayer; the PERMIT outranks the BLOCK",
  "who_is_tessera": "a Windows component, not MXC: the string 'Tessera Sandbox' is in System32 processmodel.dll and absent from every exe and dll in both MXC builds' directories (ASCII, UTF-16 and GUID-byte search); MXC 525d0f25 docs/logging-access-denied.md:260-264 calls Tessera an internal Windows component and names these provider and sublayer GUIDs; its reason code 103 is proxyContainment",
  "mxc_statements_about_wfp": "MXC 525d0f25 docs/logging-access-denied.md:248 'MXC does not coordinate with WFP directly'; docs/backends/process-container/networking.md:37-50 'PSEC blocks outbound with WFP'; base_container_helpers.rs:94-97 proxy mode deliberately omits internetClient",
  "firewall_rules_created_0": "holds: it counts MXC-authored Windows Firewall rules, not these filters",
  "capability_only_reading": "does not hold: direct egress is also under a per-run, SID-keyed proxy-containment BLOCK, in addition to the missing internetClient capability",
  "identical_shape_in_both_arms": true
 },
 "which_layer_gave_10013": {
  "b3_second_loopback_listener_port_18111": "attributable to the Tessera BLOCK by inference from the filter shape, not observed: b2 to the same address on port 18110 succeeded; the only run-SID filters with a port condition are the two Tessera PERMITs for 18110; no filter mentions 18111",
  "b4i_gateway_and_b4ii_1.1.1.1": "not distinguishable: the missing network capability and the Tessera BLOCK would each refuse",
  "not_observed": "no WFP net-event (classify-drop with filterId) capture and no captureDenials reason codes (App Isolation 1 against Tessera 103) were recorded"
 },
